\pard\sa120
\pard\qj\sa120\sl276\slmult1 \par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl276\slmult1 The predictive accuracy of each model on both subsets is summarised in Table 3. A clear and consistent pattern emerges: the ensemble learners outperform the single trees on every metric, and within the ensembles the boosted models surpass the bagged ones. XGBoost gives the best testing performance, with R\u178? = 0.962, RMSE = 3.41 MPa, MAE = 2.58 MPa, MAPE = 7.2%, and NSE = 0.961, closely followed by GBRT and random forest. The single CART tree is the weakest learner, with a testing R\u178? of 0.861 and an RMSE almost twice that of XGBoost, while REPTree and M5P occupy the middle ground.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl276\slmult1 {\fs20 \b Table 3  }{\fs20 Training and testing performance of the eight models (CS in MPa).}\par
\pard
